juno-drivers (0.5.48.2+diamon4) unstable; urgency=low

  * New binary package clevo-keyboard-dkms: the patched Clevo keyboard
    driver, bundled at build time from the tuxedo-keyboard checkout pinned at
    8d62d12 (dkms.conf PACKAGE_VERSION 4.6.2+diamon1), installs dpkg-owned
    under /usr/src/clevo-keyboard-4.6.2+diamon1 and registers with dkms
    through dh_dkms snippets only. It Conflicts/Replaces/Provides
    clevo-keyboard, deposing Juno's package whose postinst cp'd an unowned
    payload into /usr/src and whose prerm glob-rm'd it on removal. The
    historical /etc/modprobe.d/clevo_keyboard.conf ships as a conffile of the
    new package.
  * juno-drivers-diamon now Recommends clevo-keyboard-dkms in place of
    clevo-keyboard.

 -- Marco Barbone <mbarbone@flatironinstitute.org>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 04:54:15 -0400

juno-drivers (0.5.48.2+diamon3) unstable; urgency=low

  * The GRUB drop-in appends to GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX instead of overwriting the
    admin's value, and stays sourceable after `apt remove` deletes the helper
    it runs (the conffile used to survive removal and break grub-mkconfig
    under set -e). test-install.sh carries the control for both directions.
  * Dropped the flatpak integration: flatpak leaves Depends and postinst no
    longer adds the flathub remote. The old remote-add fetched from the
    network, so an offline configure died under set -e; this fork does not
    want flatpak in the first place.
  * Dropped /etc/initramfs-tools/resume: mkinitramfs never sources that path.
    rm_conffile in the maintscript cleans it off upgraded systems.
  * postrm removes the model-gated files postinst drops (juno-audio-fix.conf,
    restore-i2c-hid, 60-nj70au-touchpad.conf) and, on purge, the NUC10 line
    postinst appends to /etc/pulse/default.pa.
  * Resynced juno-grub-cmdline with upstream juno-grub 0.1.24: X4HP4NAL gains
    atkbd.reset in its own arm, S13/junotab4 gains the panel-orientation
    parameter. The upstream watch now also reads juno-grub's changelog.
  * Deleted dead payload (restart-audio, restore-ethernet-connection,
    disable-cpu-turbo.service, the empty install/ dir), the empty skel dirs,
    and the bit-rotted uninstall target. juno-cpufreq.rules installs 0644.
  * New maintainer: Marco Barbone. Giovanni Caligaris stays credited as
    XSBC-Original-Maintainer; Homepage points at the fork.

 -- Marco Barbone <mbarbone@flatironinstitute.org>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 06:38:03 -0400

juno-drivers (0.5.48.2+diamon2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Recommend the Clevo keyboard and fan packages. Recommends is what protects
    a package from autoremove (Suggests does not), and Depends is wrong here:
    clevo-keyboard's postinst writes to sysfs, which a read-only-/sys
    container must not be asked to survive.

 -- Marco Barbone <mbarbone@flatironinstitute.org>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:10:00 -0400

juno-drivers (0.5.48.2+diamon1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Merged the split into one package: juno-drivers-diamon now carries the
    whole driver payload plus the local GRUB cmdline and CPU policy. It
    Provides/Conflicts/Replaces juno-drivers, juno-drivers-local and juno-grub,
    so apt swaps every earlier layout.

 -- Marco Barbone <mbarbone@flatironinstitute.org>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 18:01:44 -0400

juno-drivers (0.5.48.1+diamon1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Renamed the local suffix from +localN to +diamonN and the package
    juno-drivers-local to juno-drivers-diamon, carrying Conflicts/Replaces/
    Provides on the old name so apt swaps it out. The upstream part gained .1
    because +diamon1 would otherwise sort below the installed +local1.

 -- Marco Barbone <mbarbone@flatironinstitute.org>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 14:42:56 -0400

juno-drivers (0.5.48+local1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Rebased onto upstream 0.5.48~debian (adds GNOME logout button).
  * Added libhidapi-hidraw0 and libhidapi-libusb0 runtime dependencies (new in
    upstream 0.5.47).
  * Retained the split juno-drivers / juno-drivers-local design.
  * Retained the PPD-aware juno-cpufreq.rules gating (skip the cpufreq udev
    symlink when power-profiles-daemon is present).
  * Kept the local dependency policy; juno-pp remains dropped and was not
    reintroduced by upstream's Depends/Recommends reorganization.
  * Dropped the juno-archive-keyring Depends: diamondinoia-repo-juno carries
    the same source and key, hash-pinned.
  * Dropped the Recommends (gaudible, geoclue-position, juno-wallpaper,
    memtest86+, steam-devices). juno-info stays.
  * postinst runs systemctl offline and guards glib-compile-schemas, so the
    package also configures in a container, which is where CI tests it.

